id: pm-todos-zgwg
title: Seven publish-attestation bypasses stayed open because the caret range floated and the lockfile did not
description: "This repository launches the canonical publish-attestation auditor from pm-ops rather than vendoring it, and declared the dependency as a caret range, so it read as tracking the canonical implementation. It was not: npm ci installs the lockfile, and the lockfile pinned pm-ops 2026.9.7. Measured with the 38-case bypass corpus against this repository's own verify(), the locked version admits seven fail-open constructions that were closed upstream two releases earlier. Raising the lock to 2026.9.9 makes the same launcher report clean with no change to scripts/verify-release-publish-attestation.ts."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-10T21:57:33.279Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-10T22:05:04.425Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-10T21:57:39.589Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-10T21:57:39.589Z"
claim_principal: claude-orchestrator
author: claude-orchestrator
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-10T22:05:04.424Z",claude-orchestrator,"Greptile raised a correct P2 on the first push: the bump closed seven fail-open cases but nothing in this repository exercised them, so a later lockfile change could restore them silently. Added two consumer-level tests to test/verify-release-publish-attestation.test.ts. The first runs all seven constructions through auditPublishAttestation from the installed pm-ops and asserts each is refused; it asserts behaviour rather than a version number, so it also fails against a regressed future release that a version floor would accept. The second is the positive control: a readable --provenance binding must still pass, without which the first test would pass against an auditor that refuses everything. Revert-check: downgrading pm-ops to 2026.9.7 turns the first test RED with 'the installed pm-ops auditor accepted the nonliteral-overwrite construction as attested' while the control stays green; restoring 2026.9.9 returns the suite to 205 of 205."
files[2]{path,scope}:
  package-lock.json,project
  package.json,project
tests[2]:
  - command: npm test
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 1800
    provenance:
      author: claude-orchestrator
      created_at: "2026-09-10T21:57:36.960Z"
      source_kind: local_mutation
      source_ref: security/close-seven-attestation-bypasses-via-pm-ops-2026-9-9
    assert_stdout_contains[1]: pass 203
    note: Suite unchanged by the pm-ops bump; the count assertion fails if the suite shrinks
  - command: node --test test/verify-release-publish-attestation.test.ts
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 600
    provenance:
      author: claude-orchestrator
      created_at: "2026-09-10T22:05:01.284Z"
      source_kind: local_mutation
      source_ref: security/close-seven-attestation-bypasses-via-pm-ops-2026-9-9
    assert_stdout_contains[1]: the installed auditor refuses every known fail-open provenance handoff
    note: Consumer-level regression guard; verified to FAIL against pm-ops 2026.9.7 and pass at 2026.9.9
close_reason: "Raised pm-ops from a locked 2026.9.7 to 2026.9.9. Measured on this repository with scripts/attest-corpus/check.sh, which runs the 38-case corpus through this repository's own verify(): before the bump it admitted nonliteral-overwrite, nonliteral-overwrite-cmdsub, quoted-metachar-value, single-quoted-metachar-value, multiword-unreadable-tail, quoted-paren-in-substitution and unterminated-substitution; after the bump it reports clean. scripts/verify-release-publish-attestation.ts is unchanged, so the difference is entirely the installed canonical implementation. npm test passes 203 of 203."
body: ""
